course: dictionary
lesson: 3972
title: Ga: a short form, a symbol, or a piece of a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ga is not a normal English word on its own. You will meet it in a few different places, and the clues show which one you have. «Atlanta, GA» is an address, so GA is a short form for Georgia, a state in the United States.
explain: In science, Ga is a chemical symbol. It stands for gallium, a soft silver metal that melts in your hand. Chemical symbols are short letters for elements, so you write Ga with a capital G and a small a.
explain: Be careful with a word that only contains the letters ga. «Garage is a French word» does not use ga as a word. The letters are only part of garage, and the sentence shows how it is said: "ga-RAZH" in French, "GARR-idge" in British English.
explain: Ga can also be slang or baby talk. To «go ga-ga» over something means to like it very much, and a baby babbling says «goo goo ga ga». Always check the sentence first, because the clues tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Ga is a short form, a symbol, or a piece of a longer word, not a normal word on its own.
fact: GA is the short form for Georgia, a state in the south-eastern United States, used in addresses.
fact: Ga is the chemical symbol for gallium, a soft silver metal that melts in your hand.
fact: To «go ga-ga» means to become very excited and silly about something.
fact: «Goo goo ga ga» is baby talk, and a baby is not using a real word when it says it.
exercise: In «Atlanta, GA», what does GA stand for? | A kind of garage | *Georgia, a state in the United States | A large green park | Gallium, a silver metal
exercise: What is Ga the chemical symbol for? | A red gas that burns | A metal called tin | *A soft silver metal called gallium | A blue liquid used in paint
exercise: Does the sentence «Garage is a French word» use ga as a word on its own? | Yes, ga means garage | Yes, ga means French | No, but ga means very excited | *No, ga is only part of the word garage
test: A baby says «goo goo ga ga». What is this? | A short form for a US state | A chemical symbol for a metal | A French word for garage | *Baby talk, not a real word
test: Leo says, «I go ga-ga over this new game.» What does he mean? | He is reading an address | He is confused and unwell | He feels very cold | *He is very excited and likes it a lot
exam: Which sentence uses ga as a short form for a US state? | «The gallium melted in my hand.» | «Goo goo ga ga, said the baby.» | *«She lives in Atlanta, GA.» | «Garage is a French word.»
